<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Walashma dynasty</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Walashma</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Walashma dynasty was a Muslim ruling family of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/horn-of-africa">Horn of Africa</a> that governed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ifat-sultanate">Ifat Sultanate</a> and then the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adal-sultanate">Adal Sultanate</a>. After Ifat's defeat by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a> around 1410, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sabr-ad-din-iii">Sabr ad-Din III</a> re-established the dynasty's state at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zeila">Zeila</a> around 1415, founding Adal. In the sixteenth century real power passed to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahmad-ibn-ibrahim-al-ghazi">Imam Ahmad</a> ibn Ibrahim al-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghazi">Ghazi</a>, who kept Walashma sultans as figureheads.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/walashma-dynasty.jpg" alt="Walashma dynasty" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: FDRMRZUSA · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Adal_Sultanate.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The Adal Sultanate was founded around 1415 CE by Sabr ad-Din III, a prince of the <b>Walashma dynasty</b> who returned from exile in Yemen after the catastrophic defeat of its predecessor state, the Ifat Sultanate.</blockquote><a href="/empire/adal-sultanate">Adal Sultanate · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>Ifat was ruled by the <b>Walashma</b> sultans from their capital in eastern Shewa, and later from the Harar plateau and Zeila.</blockquote><a href="/empire/sultanate-of-ifat">Sultanate of Ifat · Governance &amp; Law</a></li><li><blockquote>The <b>Walasma</b> dynasty that followed carried on Muslim power in the region for two more centuries.</blockquote><a href="/state/sultanate-of-shewa">Sultanate of Shewa</a></li></ul></section>
